Event Loop — cross-platform I/O multiplexing for TML.

Provides a high-level abstraction over WSAPoll (Windows) and epoll (Linux)
for building event-driven servers, proxies, and networking tools.

# Architecture

```text
┌──────────────────────────────────────┐
│              NetEventLoop               │
│  ┌─────────┐  ┌──────────────────┐   │
│  │  Poller  │  │  Token → Source  │   │
│  │ (epoll/  │  │    mapping      │   │
│  │ WSAPoll) │  │                  │   │
│  └─────────┘  └──────────────────┘   │
└──────────────────────────────────────┘
        │                  │
   poll_wait()        on_event()
        │                  │
   ┌────▼────┐       ┌────▼────┐
   │ POLLIN  │       │ Handler │
   │ POLLOUT │       │ callback│
   │ POLLERR │       │         │
   └─────────┘       └─────────┘
```

# Example — Echo Server

```tml
use std::net::eventloop::{NetEventLoop, Interest, Token, Event}

let ev: NetEventLoop = NetEventLoop::new(1024)
let listener_fd: I64 = bind_and_listen(3000)
ev.register(listener_fd, Token(0), Interest::Readable)

loop (true) {
    let count: I64 = ev.poll(100)
    var i: I64 = 0
    loop (i < count) {
        let event: Event = ev.event_at(i)
        if event.token() == 0 {
            // Accept new connection
            let fd: I64 = accept(listener_fd)
            ev.register(fd, Token(next_token), Interest::Readable)
        } else if event.is_readable() {
            // Handle read
        } else if event.is_writable() {
            // Handle write
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
}
ev.destroy()
```

TCP networking primitives. // v2

This module provides TCP socket types for reliable, ordered, connection-based
byte stream communication.

# Types

- [`TcpListener`] - Listens for incoming TCP connections
- [`TcpStream`] - A connected TCP socket for reading and writing
- [`TcpIncoming`] - Iterator over incoming connections

# Example: Echo Server

```tml
use std::net::tcp::{TcpListener, TcpStream}
use std::net::{SocketAddr, Ipv4Addr}

func main() -> Outcome[(), NetError] {
    // Bind to localhost:8080
    let addr = SocketAddr::new(Ipv4Addr::LOCALHOST, 8080)
    let listener = TcpListener::bind(addr)!

    print("Listening on {}\n", listener.local_addr())

    // Accept connections
    loop (true) {
        let (mut stream, peer) = listener.accept()!
        print("Connection from {}\n", peer)

        // Echo data back
        var buf: [U8; 1024] = [0; 1024]
        loop (true) {
            let n = stream.read(mut ref buf)!
            if n == 0 { break }
            stream.write_all(ref buf[0..n])!
        }
    }
}
```

Transport Layer Security (TLS) for encrypted network communication.

This module provides TLS client and server support built on OpenSSL,
enabling secure communication over TCP sockets.

# Types

- [`TlsContext`] - Configuration for TLS connections (wraps SSL_CTX)
- [`TlsStream`] - An encrypted TLS connection (wraps SSL)
- [`TlsVersion`] - TLS protocol version constants
- [`TlsVerifyMode`] - Certificate verification modes

# Example: TLS Client

```tml
use std::net::{TcpStream, SocketAddr, Ipv4Addr}
use std::net::tls::{TlsContext, TlsStream}

func main() -> Outcome[(), NetError] {
    // Create TCP connection
    let addr = SocketAddr::new(Ipv4Addr::new(93, 184, 216, 34), 443)
    let tcp = TcpStream::connect(addr)!

    // Wrap with TLS using socket fd
    let ctx = TlsContext::client()!
    let raw = tcp.as_raw_socket()
    let mut tls = TlsStream::connect(ctx, raw.handle, "example.com")!

    // Send HTTP request
    tls.write_str("GET / HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: example.com\r\n\r\n")!

    // Read response
    var buf: [U8; 4096] = [0; 4096]
    let n = tls.read(mut ref buf)!
    print("Received {} bytes\n", n)

    tls.shutdown()!
}
```

